  "docs": {
    "purpose": "A testing bench where an operator pretends to be a tradesperson at a given map location and sees exactly which leads the backend would serve them, with the reasoning behind each result exposed. Results can be saved to the watchlist from here. The page also carries two signposts onward - to the standalone watchlist tool and to the detail inspectors.",
    "data_story": "It reads nothing from the database directly. Every value arrives through 2 contracts: `/api/admin/leads/test-feed`, `/api/admin/leads/watchlist`. Behind those contracts, the data comes from `admin_watchlist`, `coa_applications`, `cost_estimates`, `entities`, `entity_projects`, `lead_trades`, `lead_views`, `neighbourhoods`, `permit_trades`, `permits`, `pg_extension`, `trade_forecasts`, `trades` and `wsib_registry`, and writes land on `admin_watchlist`.",
    "under_126": "**REBUILD** — it drives writes, so a client decision has to be re-homed on the server before the projection can be honest. It renders through the SEARCH renderer (declared debounce, minimum query length, rate bucket and candidate shape), reading by reference: `/api/admin/leads/test-feed`, `/api/admin/leads/watchlist`. Its `owns.components[]` declares `src/components/admin/TestFeedTool.tsx`."
  },
